302
00:51:55.510 --> 00:52:15.300
Keith Kowal (Hedera Hashgraph LLC): those projects are probably not security sensitive, but I have nominated some other projects which I think are security sensitive, and that's at the appendix of this, like things like the consensus node, the JSON RPC relay, the, the SDKs. I would say… I would argue that these are all security sensitive, in that if you have a malicious maintainer or committer.

303
00:52:15.300 --> 00:52:19.630
Keith Kowal (Hedera Hashgraph LLC): They could, depending on how you have it set up, they could potentially do a lot of damage.

304
00:52:21.460 --> 00:52:40.250
Keith Kowal (Hedera Hashgraph LLC): there are some real-world precedents for this. There have been hacks where, like, someone puts… invests time and effort to do contributions to a repo, they get trust, they become a committer or maintainer, and then they do bad things in the repo. So this is not theoretical, and I would just say in the case of Hiero.

305
00:52:40.250 --> 00:52:42.580
Keith Kowal (Hedera Hashgraph LLC): Because there's, again, so much money at stake.

