00:53:38.830 --> 00:53:45.529
Keith Kowal (Hedera Hashgraph LLC): Between PRs and releases, in terms of our security approach. Also, just let me say that, like,

311
00:53:45.530 --> 00:54:01.080
Keith Kowal (Hedera Hashgraph LLC): I, you know, the tussle in this is that we don't want to slow down momentum. Like, we don't want to put in, like, you know, we could say, oh, every PR needs 5 maintainer checks from 5 different maintainers. I mean, that would be great from a security perspective, but that's terrible from a velocity perspective.

312
00:54:01.080 --> 00:54:05.619
Keith Kowal (Hedera Hashgraph LLC): So everything tries to balance, like, velocity with security.

