00:59:04.710 --> 00:59:23.340
Keith Kowal (Hedera Hashgraph LLC): So I think that's one aspect of this, is the identity verification at nomination. Another one would be that GPG key registration. Now, we already have GPG keys. This is trying to prevent another angle of attack. We all have GitHub accounts. I think for most of us, if our GitHub account is hacked.

340
00:59:23.340 --> 00:59:36.869
Keith Kowal (Hedera Hashgraph LLC): the hacker can go in and change our GPG keys, and then continue to sign releases or PRs. I think we kind of need to lock that down, in that what I'm suggesting is that we need a GPG registration list.

